5-2a845f22f0d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514484 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=4:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-4I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514515 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b55ab94-44ca-5e5f-8316-aab35be9951d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514515 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186378969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514542 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514542 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ebe10e4f-7dda-5f32-aa46-5a154ec9adc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514542 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514543 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759